# Suite asm (D-16 to D-19, plan 07-03): the project mini-assembler ivs_asm against the hand-assembled
# listings. asm.twin-<id>: the twin source under tests/asm/twins/ assembles to words that ivs_pack
# --dump-words reads exactly as it reads the committed hand listing (the third outside check of the
# encoding table, D-18); the four twins cover the boot stub (22 words), diag-cpu-1 (56), diag-ctrl-psg-1 (89)
# and diag-stic-1 (133, its pattern table written as DECLE data words): 300 hand-typed words in all.
# asm.repeat: one twin assembled twice gives byte-identical listings (determinism of the tool).
# asm.pairs.<class>: tests/asm/pairs.txt, the flat copy of the hand-derived asm and word pairs of the Phase 2
# vectors plus three hand cases (the second outside check of the encoding table, D-18), assembled by one
# ivs_asm --pairs process; one case per row family, ok when every pair of the family assembled to its words.
# asm.judge.mutated-pair: the same self-control for the pairs comparison (one expected word changed).
# asm.judge.mutated-twin: self-control of the words comparison; passes only when it fails on a twin
# with one register changed and the diff shows that one word.
asm.twin-boot-stub
asm.twin-diag-cpu-1
asm.twin-diag-ctrl-psg-1
asm.twin-diag-stic-1
asm.repeat
asm.judge.mutated-twin
asm.pairs.move
asm.pairs.alu
asm.pairs.imm
asm.pairs.shift
asm.pairs.branch
asm.pairs.jump
asm.pairs.stack
asm.pairs.sdbd
asm.pairs.control
asm.judge.mutated-pair
